From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Remove the AP_VLAN of a WDS station from the entry that
 created it

ap_free_sta() removes the AP_VLAN of a station whose entry holds
WLAN_STA_WDS, or WLAN_STA_MULTI_AP on a backhaul BSS with wds_sta. These
flags describe the entry, not the AP_VLAN, and the AP_VLAN can outlive
the entry state they come from:

- A new authentication keeps the entry and its AP_VLAN for the next
  association. If that association is refused, check_multi_ap() has
  cleared WLAN_STA_MULTI_AP, so the free of the entry leaves the
  AP_VLAN. This also holds for a station that is no MLD.
- On an AP MLD, only the link station that received the 4-address frame
  holds WLAN_STA_WDS. If it is freed while another link station stays,
  no link station removes the AP_VLAN of a plain WDS non-AP MLD.
- With the rule of hostap commit 7561cfa1ea9a ("WDS: Interface removal
  in MLO cases"), a link station removes the AP_VLAN where no other
  link BSS of the AP MLD has an entry for the address. An
  entry of a new authentication counts as such an entry. The station of
  a link BSS that left the AP MLD is not found by the others, so the
  removal of the association link removes the AP_VLAN twice: once from
  the link station that sees no partner, and again from the station of
  the removed link BSS when it is freed.

Mark the entry on which hostapd created or enabled again the AP_VLAN,
and remove the AP_VLAN only from that entry. The mark is set also where
hostapd_set_wds_sta() fails, because the driver can create the AP_VLAN
and then fail to add it to the bridge or to move the station to it.
Where the marked link station of a non-AP MLD is freed and another link
station of the MLD stays, the mark passes to that station. A link BSS
that left the AP MLD still reaches the remaining links through
hapd->mld. Upstream main 741d70dd8e32 decides by the flags as before.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -9164,6 +9164,7 @@ skip_update:
 			   MAC2STR(sta->addr), sta->aid);
 		ret = hostapd_set_wds_sta(hapd, ifname_wds, sta->addr,
 					  sta->aid, 1);
+		sta->wds_vlan = 1;
 		if (!ret)
 			hostapd_set_wds_encryption(hapd, sta, ifname_wds);
 	}
@@ -9534,6 +9535,7 @@ void ieee802_11_rx_from_unknown(struct h
 			sta->flags |= WLAN_STA_WDS;
 			ret = hostapd_set_wds_sta(hapd, ifname_wds,
 						  sta->addr, sta->aid, 1);
+			sta->wds_vlan = 1;
 			if (!ret)
 				hostapd_set_wds_encryption(hapd, sta,
 							   ifname_wds);
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -402,11 +402,7 @@ void ap_free_sta(struct hostapd_data *ha
 	ap_sta_set_authorized(hapd, sta, 0);
 	hostapd_set_sta_flags(hapd, sta);
 
-	if ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_WDS) ||
-	    (sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MULTI_AP &&
-	     (hapd->conf->multi_ap & BACKHAUL_BSS) &&
-	     hapd->conf->wds_sta &&
-	     !(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_WPS))) {
+	if (sta->wds_vlan) {
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
 		if (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta)) {
 			struct hostapd_data *phapd;
@@ -418,6 +414,7 @@ void ap_free_sta(struct hostapd_data *ha
 
 				psta = ap_get_sta(phapd, sta->addr);
 				if (psta) {
+					psta->wds_vlan = 1;
 					remove = false;
 					break;
 				}
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.h
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.h
@@ -166,6 +166,7 @@ struct sta_info {
 	unsigned int ecsa_supported:1;
 	unsigned int added_unassoc:1;
 	unsigned int pending_wds_enable:1;
+	unsigned int wds_vlan:1; /* owns the AP_VLAN of the station */
 	unsigned int power_capab:1;
 	unsigned int agreed_to_steer:1;
 	unsigned int hs20_t_c_filtering:1;
